            0.066
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Geometric Twins"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.664,
            0.107
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Similarly, the sides AB and BC are equal. So "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{A} = \\angle \\mathrm{C}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.108,
            0.847,
            0.146
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, all the three angles of an equilateral triangle are equal, just like their sides."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.155,
            0.46,
            0.178
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What could be their measures?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.188,
            0.67,
            0.246
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As the three angles should add up to 180°, we have 3 × angle in an equilateral triangle = 180°. So each angle is 60°."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.254,
            0.419,
            0.278
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Verify this by construction."
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.287,
            0.846,
            0.326
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, just using the notion of congruence, we have deduced that the angles of an equilateral triangle are all 60°."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.326,
            0.847,
            0.384
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Congruent Triangles in Real Life:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Congruent triangles can be seen in various constructions and designs from ancient to modern times. Here are a few examples."
            }
          ]
        },
